  "authoringNotes": [
    "Chains specify regional connectivity goals. They are not straight-line navigable tracks; root must generate and sweep-check the resulting water routes against the game coast.",
    "Magellan Strait, the Beagle Channel, Chacao and the Aysen/Natales fjords may be closed by simplified Natural Earth geometry. Do not move a named berth beyond 50 km or cut unrelated land to force a route.",
    "Cape Horn to Fildes is a genuine long open-water crossing. There is no intermediate real island selected for refuelling. Preserve an infeasible result for boats whose actual conservative range cannot cover it.",
    "Puerto Chacabuco to Puerto Natales is another long stage; it must not be made feasible by understating distance or fuel. Puerto Eden is a possible later real coastal addition if needed, outside this bounded 14-location bundle.",
    "Antarctic country labels describe the continent and do not encode territorial claims."
  ],
